-- KNOWN LIMIT, pinned so that it cannot change silently. A decode the rules make
-- into a record declared under a heading in an IMPORTED module names the type
-- bare (`JSONDECODE `Paint Order`: coats`), while the WITH entry of the same
-- record carries the heading (`WITH `Stock items`.`Paint Order`: coats`). The
-- headings of an imported module do not reach the evaluator: it receives the
-- imports' DECLAREs as a flat list. A record declared under a heading in THIS
-- module is named behind it (batch-typically-decode-*.l4).

IMPORT `batch-typically-decode-import-lib`

GIVEN s IS A STRING
GIVETH AN EITHER STRING `Paint Order`
parseOrder s MEANS JSONDECODE s

GIVETH A NUMBER
`decoded coats` MEANS CONSIDER parseOrder "{}"
    WHEN RIGHT o THEN o's coats
    WHEN LEFT e THEN 0

@export default coats
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE coats amount IS (`Paint Order` WITHAL)'s coats PLUS `decoded coats` PLUS amount
